{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786476530,"nonce":"Ndp6UfumwsAsSxTCGHctaMejEj8=","message":"Fixed in 90ff979. The filter now lives in the replay emit loop, so Interest.Matches is the single definition and live and replay cannot disagree. Deliberately NOT in the SQL WHERE: resource is a column but the alert_id/group_id narrowing comes from the payload via ScopeOf, so SQL could only be half the filter; MaxReplayRows would stop bounding anything; and ReplayResult.LastSeq would become the highest MATCHING seq rather than the highest in the gap, which is the cursor trap the ticket named. That trap is closed with a bare id-only SSE block, which advances lastEventId without dispatching a message. Known residual, out of scope: the live path has the same cursor lag in miniature; it now self-heals on reconnect.","files":null}]}